  <img decoding="async" width="696" height="392" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="'Bitcoin Is Dead'- Crypto Market Carnage Invokes Haters and BTC Obituaries" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries-760x428.jpg 760w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitcoin-is-dead-crypto-market-carnage-invokes-haters-and-btc-obituaries.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 696px) 100vw, 696px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>Digital currency markets have shed billions in value over the past week and during the market carnage, bitcoin haters have come out in flocks. Moreover, according to numerous crypto skeptics, bitcoin has officially died 21 times this year and this week’s downturn is sure to provide another eulogy.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Bitcoin Haters Step Out to Troll Crypto Proponents
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    On April 14, 2021, the price of bitcoin (BTC) tapped an all-time price high at $64,895 per unit, and then slid to a low of $30,066 a touch over a month later on May 19. That’s a percentage loss of 53% down from the high.
  </p>
  
  <blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true">
    <p lang="es" dir="ltr">
      Tesla has 💎 🙌
    </p>
    
    <p>
      — Elon Musk (@elonmusk) May 19, 2021
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    BTC has regained some of the losses it has taken on Wednesday morning, but is still down quite a bit from yesterday’s price highs. Market trauma like this causes numerous bitcoin haters to come out of the woodwork, as many feel the need to explain to the public that crypto is nothing more than speculative ‘tulip mania.’
  </p>
  
  <p>
    On Wednesday, the bitcoin hater Nouriel Roubini tweeted about BTC after the prices plunged to new 2021 lows.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    “Bitcoin falls more than 40% from its peak in less than one month. Which institutional investors are reckless enough to invest in such a risky and volatile pseudo-asset with no intrinsic value? Roubini asked. “They should be fired on the spot if undertaking such a reckless speculative gamble,” the skeptic further added.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-460233 size-full" title="'Bitcoin Is Dead'- Crypto Market Carnage Invokes Haters and BTC Obituaries" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38.jpg" alt="'Bitcoin Is Dead'- Crypto Market Carnage Invokes Haters and BTC Obituaries" width="2416" height="1316" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38.jpg 2416w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-300x163.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-1024x558.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-768x418.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-1536x837.jpg 1536w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-2048x1116.jpg 2048w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-696x379.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-1392x758.jpg 1392w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-1068x582.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-771x420.jpg 771w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-wed_19_may_10_48_38-1920x1046.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2416px) 100vw, 2416px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    The gold bug and economist Peter Schiff believes that this is a full-fledged “bitcoin bear market.”
  </p>
  
  <p>
    “The most bearish aspect of the Bitcoin bear market is that it’s been slow and steady, at least by Bitcoin standards,” Schiff’s tweet noted on Wednesday. “So far there hasn’t been a crash that would indicate capitulation. Instead, Bitcoin bulls remain steadfast, their faith unshaken as they confidently buy every dip.”
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-460237" title="'Bitcoin Is Dead'- Crypto Market Carnage Invokes Haters and BTC Obituaries" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead.jpg" alt="'Bitcoin Is Dead'- Crypto Market Carnage Invokes Haters and BTC Obituaries" width="611" height="343" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead-768x432.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/dead-760x428.jpg 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 611px) 100vw, 611px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Meanwhile, droves of BTC supporters are unshaken it seems, and many believe the bad times will soon be over. “For those new to crypto, please let me introduce our old friend honey badger. Honey badger don’t care,” Watchdog Capital’s Bruce Fenton said on Wednesday.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    “Not concerned,” the host of the Youtube show ‘Colin Talks Crypto’ stressed. “Bull run is still on. I sold a small bit of BTC and ETH yesterday. Going to re-buy lower,” the Youtuber added on Wednesday.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    2021 Has Seen Approximately 21 Bitcoin Obituaries
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    2021 has seen all-time highs (ATH) as far as a number of crypto assets are concerned and BTC spiked 2x higher than 2017’s previous ATH. However, 2021 has seen a number of “Bitcoin Obituary Stats,” as approximately 21 deaths have been recorded on the web portal 99bitcoins.com.
  </p>
  
  <blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true">
    <p lang="en" dir="ltr">
      So now that #Bitcoin is dead again what are you all up to?
    </p>
    
    <p>
      — Ben Kaufman (@_benkaufman) May 19, 2021
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    BTC had a recent obituary published on May 18, 2021, which was written by The Independent author Tim Mullaney. The death sentence called “The Harsh Truth About Crypto” explains why Mullaney truly believes BTC is “basically nothing.” The Independent author adds:
  </p>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      <em><strong>And that’s why the world’s most-traded cryptocurrency is worth basically nothing… Don’t even start on the notion that bitcoin is a currency or a store of value, or a hedge against inflation. The unstable price chart belies all of those notions, as does exposure to bitcoin advocates, none of whom will be running the Federal Reserve soon.</strong></em>
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    Mullaney’s opinion highlights that bitcoin isn’t much of a ‘revolution’ unless someone can tell him what the “revolutionary technology does in the real world.” The author concludes that “Amusing Elon doesn’t count. For crypto, t’aint much.”
  </p>
  
  <p>
    In addition to Mullaney’s opinion editorial, there’s 20 more obituaries that stress bitcoin is sitting in a casket while this article is written. At the time of publication, at 11:30 a.m. (EST) on Wednesday, bitcoin (BTC) is exchanging hands for $36,979 per unit.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about the recent hate toward bitcoin’s market downturn and the 21 bitcoin obituaries published on 99bitcoins? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below.</strong></em>
  </p>
</div>
